      "content": "That's definitely moving in the right direction with the 0.85, but I'm still seeing a lot of \"regret\" and \"less-than-ideal\" which is dragging the sentiment down. \n\nTo be honest, the client is really pushing for a version that radiates hospitality and positivity. They want the response to feel like a \"bright spot\" in the customer's day, even though we're addressing a problem. If we can get that score above 0.95, it'll help the client feel confident that we're successfully pivoting the narrative from \"bad service\" to \"amazing recovery.\"\n\nCan you take one more crack at it? Try to use more uplifting, high-sentiment language while you address the issue. Just please, please don't go overboard and make it sound like a bubbly commercial—we still have to address the cold food and the staff issue, or it won't be a real apology. Just find that sweet spot where the positivity score is very high but it still feels like we're a real company.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
